<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cattle">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cattle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cattle are domesticated bovines kept for milk, meat, hides and draught, and in many societies as a measure of wealth. Herds were central to the economies and social structures of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> empires, whose founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changamire-dombo">Changamire Dombo</a> began as a cattle administrator, and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a>. Steppe empires such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> and Mongol empires also relied on livestock, and herded cattle caused panic among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> forces at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tondibi">Tondibi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cattle.jpg" alt="Cattle" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dr. Plamen Ivanov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bulgarian_gray_cattle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
